source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:01bb803641fd1ea0dccc0542fe6ce66d8f9b5889a071e28da077ead584549ffe","file":"preprints/A-finitely-generated-counterexample-to-the-Eilenberg-Ganea-conjecture-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex","line":15,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"2e1ee705bd97fb2d1a9f0710b1cab014c2337eb03de0032010931e0df7bf8cfc","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/A-finitely-generated-counterexample-to-the-Eilenberg-Ganea-conjecture-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:01bb803641fd1ea0dccc0542fe6ce66d8f9b5889a071e28da077ead584549ffe","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/A-finitely-generated-counterexample-to-the-Eilenberg-Ganea-conjecture-September-23-2026/build/sections/introduction.tex#L15"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nThere is a finitely generated residually finite group $G$ such that\n\\[\n \\cdim G=2,\\qquad \\gdim G=3.\n\\]\nOne may take $G$ to be the height kernel in the right-angled Artin group associated to a finite acyclic flag triangulation of the presentation complex\n\\begin{equation}\n\\label{eq:seed-presentation-intro}\n \\langle x,y\\mid x^2=y^5,\\ x^2=(xy^{-1})^3\\rangle.\n\\end{equation}\nNo two-dimensional classifying space for this $G$ exists, regardless of the number of its cells."}
